## Code Review: Null Pointer Bug in Nested Config Access

### Highest-Risk Bug

**Location:** `src/main/java/com/example/config/DataSourceFactory.java`, line 6

```java
return config.getDatabase().getJdbcUrl().trim();
```

### Root Cause

The code performs a **chained null dereference** without any null checks. Three potential null points exist:

| Expression | Potential Null Source | Result |
|------------|----------------------|--------|
| `config` | Passed as null to `buildJdbcUrl()` | NPE on `config.getDatabase()` |
| `config.getDatabase()` | Database config not set | NPE on `.getJdbcUrl()` |
| `config.getDatabase().getJdbcUrl()` | JDBC URL not configured | NPE on `.trim()` |

This is a **startup-time crash risk** — the application fails before it can start if any nested configuration is missing.

---

### Smallest Production-Safe Patch

**File: `src/main/java/com/example/config/DataSourceFactory.java`**

```java
package com.example.config;

public class DataSourceFactory {
    public String buildJdbcUrl(AppConfig config) {
        if (config == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("AppConfig must not be null");
        }
        DatabaseConfig dbConfig = config.getDatabase();
        if (dbConfig == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Database config must not be null");
        }
        String jdbcUrl = dbConfig.getJdbcUrl();
        if (jdbcUrl == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("JDBC URL must not be null");
        }
        return jdbcUrl.trim();
    }
}
```

### Why This Fix?

1. **Minimal scope** — Only touches the single method with the bug
2. **Clear error messages** — Pinpoints exactly which config is missing
3. **Fail-fast** — Fails early with a meaningful message rather than cryptic NPE
4. **No API changes** — No changes needed in callers or config classes

